From 0a1a59d99026d1e094ca7a257d162bfb581ff3e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:44:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(repair): expire a saved review request that binds no
 journal

JAM B5. ai.ubq.fi 630 (PR 999), 604 (PR 1053) and 647 (PR 1011) sat at
`review` for 15-92 hours, each with an ambiguous review_request intent
for round reviewRounds + 1 whose attempt key no review journal on the
pull request binds. observeReview takes its saved-request branch for
them and returned `review intent has no exact bound journal` on every
run: unlike the transport-failure, pending and non-terminal unavailable
branches, it never asked reviewAttemptExpired, so the attempt could not
expire and nothing ever moved.

That branch now expires after the same bound (REVIEW_BOUND_MS) and is
recovered by the same recoverExpiredReviewAttempt as every other
attempt: the saved round is counted once (the existing expired-attempt
rule: a bound review_request intent the counter never counted is
counted and cleared), its ambiguous charge stays in the ledger
unchanged, and the next round goes through the ceiling, freshness and
CI-first gates of requestReviewFor. Inside the bound nothing is written.

The bound is anchored at the attempt in flight. requestReviewFor sets
the intent on the freshly loaded record, which keeps the previous
round's wait, so 604 and 647 carry round N-1's review_pending since
beside round N's intent. reviewAttemptExpired now never starts the
bound before a review_request intent's own start (the later of the
wait's since and the intent's startedAt), in every branch: an attempt
never inherits an earlier round's deadline, and nothing expires earlier
than before. Without this the new branch, and the existing
transport-failure branch, could recover an ambiguous attempt seconds
after it was submitted and charge another round.

Replayed from the live records and every charge of each task
(tests/fixtures/repair/review-saved-request-live.json, state 3503d6ba7)
through the real cycle at the next pass: 604 requests its third and
last round, 630 (red head) goes to the CI-first gate with no review,
and 647 (four rounds spent, legacy pin 4, green, unarmed) parks with
the existing UNREVIEWED ceiling message. No refund, no new state shape,
blocker, wait or output line: everything written is what R80 writes.

The post-drain entrypoint scenario used this jam as its "unrelated
non-matrix deferral" with an intent 45 minutes old; its stuck record now
starts inside the bound (2 minutes old, beside the previous round's
older wait), so it is still that deferral and also guards the anchor.

